</style></head><body><h1>IRC channel logs</h1><h2>2025-01-18.log</h2><p><a href="/bootstrappable">back to list of logs</a></p><div id="logs"><div class="line" id="003726"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#003726" label="[00:37:26]">&lt;lrvick&gt;</a></span><span class="message">For now I cheated and let &quot;ADD&quot; extract files for me, which it weirdly has support for</span></div><div class="line" id="003744"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#003744" label="[00:37:44]">&lt;lrvick&gt;</a></span><span class="message">however that is probably not going to be compatible with all OCI implementations. Certianly not sloci-image</span></div><div class="line" id="003750"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#003750" label="[00:37:50]">&lt;lrvick&gt;</a></span><span class="message">and I don't want a hard dependency on docker.</span></div><div class="line" id="133303"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#133303" label="[13:33:03]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">nice, gtker added support for enums to M2-Planet <a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/oriansj/M2-Planet/pull/60">https://github.com/oriansj/M2-Planet/pull/60</a> </span></div><div class="line" id="143449"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#143449" label="[14:34:49]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">argh, added a few more components to tinycc-compiled linux24 kernel, recently nfs/nfsd, all of the sudden this thing crashed during boot</span></div><div class="line" id="143535"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#143535" label="[14:35:35]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">seems i was hitting a kernel-image size limit (that i increased manually some place), and it's corrupting memory at some yet unknown boundary</span></div><div class="line" id="143617"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#143617" label="[14:36:17]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">this thing does need extensive testing before, ideally before git-pushing to avoid others hitting such problems</span></div><div class="line" id="143837"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#143837" label="[14:38:37]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">max statically linked linux image size seems to be ~6.4MiB, a tad more and with 6.5MiB it crashes</span></div><div class="line" id="144140"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#144140" label="[14:41:40]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">anyway, no big problem, i'll patch build-system to issue a warning if size limit is surpassed, which i had set to 8MiB which is too much, obviously</span></div><br /></div></body></html>